          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category"} homotopy 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_2\big((\infty,1)Cat\big)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C2%29-category"} (∞,2)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Cat"} (∞,1)Cat
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            has been argued (
            %a{:href => "#RiehlVerity13"}> Riehl &amp; Verity 13
            , following
            %a{:href => "#Joyal08"} Joyal 08
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf#page=10"} p. 158
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            (in the spirit of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Gray"} John Gray
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adjointness+for+2-Categories"} formal category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            of plain
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
          %p
            For example, the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} adjoint (∞,1)-functors
            turns out to equivalently reduce to plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
            in this homotopy 2-category (
            %a{:href => "#Joyal08"} Joyal 08
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf#page=11"} p. 159
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RiehlVerity13"} Riehl &amp; Verity 13, Sec 4
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AdjunctionsAndAdjointInfinityFunctors"} below
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#AdjunctionsAndAdjointInfinityFunctors
            Adjunctions and adjoint
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
          #AdjointInfinityFunctorsInHomotopy2Category.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              An adjunction in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
                homotopy 2-category of
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              is equivalently a pair of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28infinity%2C1%29-functors"}
                  adjoint
                  = succeed "-functors" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          (
          %a{:href => "adjoint+infinity1-functor#RiehlVerity15"}> Riehl &amp; Verity 2015, Rem. 4.4.5
          ;
          = succeed ";" do
            %a{:href => "adjoint+infinity1-functor#RVElements"} Riehl &amp; Verity 2022, Prop. F.5.6
          %a{:href => "adjoint+infinity1-functor#InTheHomotopy2Category"} there
          for more).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In view of its classical analog (
              %a{:href => "adjunction#AdjunctionsInCatAreAdjointFunctors"}> this Prop.
              ), the remarkable aspect of Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointInfinityFunctorsInHomotopy2Category"}
              is that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"}
                homotopy 2-category of
                = succeed "-categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              is sufficient to detect adjointness of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-functors"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  \-functors
              = succeed "," do
                %em a priori
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C2%29-category"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,2)
                \-category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29Cat"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Cat
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{(\infty,1)}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "adjoint+infinity1-functor#RiehlVerity16"} Riehl &amp; Verity 2016, Thm. 4.3.11, 4.4.11
          %h3#RelationToHomotopy2CategoryOfCombinatorialModelCategories Relation to homotopy 2-category of model categories?
          %p
            One might expect (by the discussion
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "locally+presentable+infinity-category#PresentedByCombinatorialSimplicialModelCategories"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+2-category"} homotopy 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} locally presentable (∞,1)-categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#Joyal08"} Joyal 08
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf#page=40"} p. 348
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalent
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization+of+a+2-category"} localization of the 2-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+categories"} combinatorial model categories
            at the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
          %p
            At least for the homotopy
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (2,1)
            %a{:href => "HoCombModCat#Pavlov21"} Pavlov 2021
            and for presentable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivators"} derivators
            it is proven in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "HoCombModCat#Renaudin06"} Renaudin 2006
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} adjoint (∞,1)-functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ho%28CombModCat%29"} Ho(CombModCat)
          %h2#references References
          %p
            With
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            modeled as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %ul
            %li#Joyal08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
              , p. 158 (10 of 348) in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The theory of quasicategories and its applications
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://lists.lehigh.edu/pipermail/algtop-l/2007q4/000017.html"} Advanced Course on Simplicial Methods in Higher Categories
              %strong 45
              2, Centre de Recerca Matemàtica, Barcelona 2008 (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            and then developed further (in terms of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cosmoi"} ∞-cosmoi
          %ul
            %li#RiehlVerity13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
              = succeed "," do
                %em The 2-category theory of quasi-categories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.5144"} arXiv:1306.5144
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2015.04.021"} doi:10.1016/j.aim.2015.04.021
          %p Review and further discussion in:
          %ul
            %li#Riehl14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                , Chapter 18 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categorical+Homotopy+Theory"} Categorical Homotopy Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jhu.edu/~eriehl/cathtpy.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781107261457"} doi:10.1017/CBO9781107261457
            %li#RiehlVerity15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Fibrations and Yoneda’s lemma in an
                    = succeed "-cosmos" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
